WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.947
In one minute, you will see how many people found your contest.

00:00:03.947 --> 00:00:05.056
We start on the map.

00:00:05.957 --> 00:00:09.289
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.069 --> 00:00:13.491
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.491 --> 00:00:15.981
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:17.327
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.077 --> 00:00:21.293
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.293 --> 00:00:21.945
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.955
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.955 --> 00:00:29.173
See the three dots?

00:00:29.173 --> 00:00:29.721
Tap them.

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:33.283
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:34.977 --> 00:00:35.605
Tap Mine.

00:00:35.605 --> 00:00:37.554
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.253
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.253 --> 00:00:42.621
This is your dashboard.

00:00:44.509 --> 00:00:45.334
Tap Promote.

00:00:48.111 --> 00:00:53.417
Activity shows page visits, visits from your QR code, and how many people voted.

00:00:54.661 --> 00:00:57.100
Below, a chart shows votes for each day.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.479
Use it to see which sharing worked best.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.590
Next up: Add sponsors and logos.
